  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: b58ed87f6d683ae4380c703929b4aac3, type: 3}
  m_Name: OnGameOver
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::GameEvent
  enableDebugLogs: 0
  description: 'Raised when the game ends (player lost all lives, failed objective,
    etc.)


    Common Listeners:

    - UIManager: Show game over screen with final
    score

    - ScoreManager: Save high score, calculate statistics

    - AudioManager:
    Play game over music/sound

    - PlayerController: Disable all input

    -
    TimeManager: Slow down or stop time

    - AchievementManager: Check and unlock
    achievements

    - AnalyticsManager: Record game session data

    - LeaderboardManager:
    Submit score to leaderboard


    Use Case:

    Different from OnPlayerDied
    - this is the FINAL death that ends the game.

    If player has lives, OnPlayerDied
    fires but OnGameOver doesn''t.

    OnGameOver = no more continues, show results
    screen.'
